{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For from the top of the rocks I see him.</b> I look at their beginning and at the origin of their roots, and I see them founded and strong like these rocks and hills, through the patriarchs and matriarchs (Tanchuma)." "<b>Lo, a people that dwells alone.</b> This is what his ancestors earned for him — to dwell alone, as the Targum renders." "<b>And among the nations he is not reckoned.</b> As the Targum renders — they will not be made an end of together with the rest of the nations, as it says ״כִּי אֶעֱשֶׂה כָלָה בְּכָל הַגּוֹיִם״ (Jeremiah 30) etc.; they are not counted with the rest. Another interpretation: when they rejoice, no nation rejoices with them, as it says ״ה׳ בָּדָד יַנְחֶנּוּ״ (Deuteronomy 32); and when the nations prosper, they eat with each and every one, yet nothing is entered to their account — and this is <b>and among the nations he is not reckoned</b> (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:23.037130840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}